{"ok":true,"data":{"kind":"command","command":"brief approve","path":["brief","approve"],"summary":"Record the human's approval of the brief, bound to its text; refused while `brief check` has blockers","effect":"write","idempotency":"replay-safe","operands":[{"name":"change","valueName":"CHANGE_ID","valueType":"string","required":false,"variadic":true,"default":null,"defaultNote":"the repo's only live change","help":"The changes to approve, one answer for all, none written unless every one is approvable (default: the repo's only live change)"}],"options":[{"name":"approver","valueName":"NAME","valueType":"string","required":true,"repeatable":false,"default":null,"help":"Who approved (the human, not the agent)"},{"name":"note","valueName":"TEXT","valueType":"string","required":true,"repeatable":false,"default":null,"help":"The human's own words"},{"name":"relayed-via","valueName":"NAME","valueType":"string","required":false,"repeatable":false,"default":null,"help":"Record the human's answer on their behalf: the tool they were asked with (`ask`, `AskUserQuestion`, `chat`); an agent role may run the call only with it"},{"name":"actor","valueName":"ACTOR_ID","valueType":"string","required":false,"repeatable":false,"default":null,"defaultNote":"the CANON_ACTOR environment variable, with --relayed-via","help":"With --relayed-via, the agent's actor id (default: the CANON_ACTOR environment variable)"},{"name":"digest","valueName":"DIGEST","valueType":"string","required":false,"repeatable":true,"default":null,"help":"With --relayed-via, the digest `canon brief show --body` showed the human, as `<change>=<sha256:digest>`, once per change; a brief whose digest differs is refused"},{"name":"repo","valueName":"DIR","valueType":"path","required":false,"repeatable":false,"default":null,"defaultNote":"the nearest ancestor directory holding a canon.yaml","flagOnly":true,"help":"The repo to act on (default: the nearest ancestor directory holding a canon.yaml)"},{"name":"json","valueType":"switch","required":false,"repeatable":false,"default":false,"flagOnly":true,"help":"Output JSON instead of the human-readable form"},{"name":"input","valueName":"JSON|FILE|-","valueType":"string","required":false,"repeatable":false,"default":null,"flagOnly":true,"help":"The arguments as JSON: an object (one run) or an array / NDJSON file or `-` (a batch); keys are the option names in camelCase, `operands` an array"},{"name":"as","valueName":"ROLE","valueType":"enum","possibleValues":["planner","implementer","reviewer","orchestrator"],"required":false,"repeatable":false,"default":null,"flagOnly":true,"help":"The role you act as: planner, implementer, reviewer or orchestrator. Overrides `CANON_ROLE`. `schema` and `context` list only the role's commands, `status` keeps its steps, and `--role` on `evidence add` / `evidence audit` / `review scenario` / `review change` is this role unless given"}],"errors":["APPROVAL_INCOMPLETE","BATCH_INCOMPLETE","BRIEF_APPROVE_REFUSED","BRIEF_NOT_FOUND","BRIEF_UNAPPROVABLE","BRIEF_UNREADABLE","BRIEF_WRITE_FAILED","CHANGE_AMBIGUOUS","CONFIG_MISSING","CONFIG_UNREADABLE","HUMAN_ONLY","INPUT_CONFLICT","INPUT_INVALID","INPUT_TOO_LARGE","INTERNAL","NO_BRIEF","POLICY_APPROVAL_FAILED","RELAY_DIGEST_MISMATCH","SPEC_ROOTS_UNREADABLE","UNKNOWN_ROLE","USAGE","WRITE_UNAVAILABLE"],"outputs":[{"kind":"report","schemaRef":"#/schemas/BriefApproveReport","schemaVersion":"1.1","when":"one change is approved"},{"kind":"report","schemaRef":"#/schemas/BriefApproveManyReport","schemaVersion":"1.1","when":"several changes are approved in one answer"},{"kind":"report","schemaRef":"#/schemas/BatchBriefApproveReport","schemaVersion":"1.1","batch":true,"when":"--input is an array or NDJSON"}],"input":{"option":"--input","schemaRef":"#/schemas/BriefApproveInput","argumentsRef":"#/schemas/BriefApproveArguments","batch":true,"maxBytes":8388608,"maxItems":10000,"example":{"approver":"alice","note":"approved as written","operands":["add-search"]}},"examples":["canon brief approve add-search --approver alice --note \"approved as written\" --json"],"schemas":{"ApprovalEntry":{"description":"One id of an [`ApprovedMany`].","properties":{"brief":{"description":"The brief file; omitted for a `skipped` id.","type":["string","null"]},"change":{"type":"string"},"digest":{"description":"The digest the approval binds; omitted for a `failed` or `skipped` id.","type":["string","null"]},"error":{"description":"Why a `failed` id failed.","type":["string","null"]},"outcome":{"$ref":"#/schemas/Outcome"}},"required":["change","outcome"],"type":"object"},"ApprovalRelay":{"description":"How an approval reached canon when an agent recorded it for a human\n(0.32): the agent's declared role and actor, the tool the human was asked\nwith, and, where the record has no field of its own for them, the human's\nname and answer. Written only for a relayed approval; a record without it\nis the human's own.","properties":{"actor":{"description":"The agent's actor id.","type":"string"},"answer":{"description":"The human's answer as given, when the record holds it nowhere else.","type":["string","null"]},"approver":{"description":"The human's name, when the record holds it nowhere else.","type":["string","null"]},"role":{"description":"The role the recording agent declared (`--as` / `CANON_ROLE`).","type":"string"},"tool":{"description":"The tool the human was asked with (`ask`, `AskUserQuestion`, `chat`).","type":"string"}},"required":["role","actor","tool"],"type":"object"},"Approved":{"description":"What one approval recorded: the `brief approve --json` data of one id.","properties":{"approvedBy":{"type":"string"},"brief":{"type":"string"},"change":{"type":"string"},"digest":{"type":"string"},"policyApproved":{"type":"boolean"},"relay":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/schemas/ApprovalRelay"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Set when an agent recorded the approval for the human (0.32)."}},"required":["change","brief","digest","approvedBy","policyApproved"],"type":"object"},"BatchBriefApproveReport":{"description":"`Batch<Name>Report`: the `data` of a leaf run with a JSON array or NDJSON as `--input`.\n`R` is the leaf's ordinary report; the binary itself carries each element's report as JSON.","properties":{"items":{"items":{"$ref":"#/schemas/BatchItem"},"type":"array"},"nextOmitted":{"description":"How many further `meta.next` steps were left out past the limit","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"unchanged":{"description":"true when a repeat found its work already done with identical content and wrote nothing; absent otherwise","type":"boolean"},"waitingOn":{"additionalProperties":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"description":"With a declared role: how many steps each other owner holds (`human` for the steps only the human takes)","type":"object"}},"required":["items"],"title":"BatchReport","type":"object"},"BatchItem":{"description":"One element of a batch, in input order.","properties":{"data":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/schemas/Approved"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The element's ordinary report (`written`, `unchanged`, and a failure that kept one)."},"error":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/schemas/ErrorBody"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The element's ordinary error, `field` a pointer into the batch (`/items/2/scenario`)."},"index":{"description":"0-based position in the input.","format":"uint","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"status":{"$ref":"#/schemas/ItemStatus"}},"required":["index","status"],"type":"object"},"BriefApproveArguments":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"actor":{"description":"With --relayed-via, the agent's actor id (default: the CANON_ACTOR environment variable)","type":"string"},"approver":{"description":"Who approved (the human, not the agent)","type":"string"},"digest":{"description":"With --relayed-via, the digest `canon brief show --body` showed the human, as `<change>=<sha256:digest>`, once per change; a brief whose digest differs is refused","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"note":{"description":"The human's own words","type":"string"},"operands":{"description":"The changes to approve, one answer for all, none written unless every one is approvable (default: the repo's only live change)","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"relayedVia":{"description":"Record the human's answer on their behalf: the tool they were asked with (`ask`, `AskUserQuestion`, `chat`); an agent role may run the call only with it","type":"string"}},"required":["approver","note"],"title":"`canon brief approve` arguments after the --input document is merged with the command line","type":"object"},"BriefApproveInput":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"actor":{"description":"With --relayed-via, the agent's actor id (default: the CANON_ACTOR environment variable)","type":"string"},"approver":{"description":"Who approved (the human, not the agent)","type":"string"},"digest":{"description":"With --relayed-via, the digest `canon brief show --body` showed the human, as `<change>=<sha256:digest>`, once per change; a brief whose digest differs is refused","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"note":{"description":"The human's own words","type":"string"},"operands":{"description":"The changes to approve, one answer for all, none written unless every one is approvable (default: the repo's only live change)","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"relayedVia":{"description":"Record the human's answer on their behalf: the tool they were asked with (`ask`, `AskUserQuestion`, `chat`); an agent role may run the call only with it","type":"string"}},"title":"`canon brief approve` --input document","type":"object"},"BriefApproveManyReport":{"description":"`brief approve --json` data for several ids: one answer, one entry per id.","properties":{"approvals":{"items":{"$ref":"#/schemas/ApprovalEntry"},"type":"array"},"approvedBy":{"type":"string"},"nextOmitted":{"description":"How many further `meta.next` steps were left out past the limit","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"policyApproved":{"type":"boolean"},"relay":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/schemas/ApprovalRelay"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Set when an agent recorded the approvals for the human (0.32)."},"unchanged":{"description":"true when a repeat found its work already done with identical content and wrote nothing; absent otherwise","type":"boolean"},"waitingOn":{"additionalProperties":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"description":"With a declared role: how many steps each other owner holds (`human` for the steps only the human takes)","type":"object"}},"required":["approvedBy","policyApproved","approvals"],"title":"ApprovedMany","type":"object"},"BriefApproveReport":{"description":"What one approval recorded: the `brief approve --json` data of one id.","properties":{"approvedBy":{"type":"string"},"brief":{"type":"string"},"change":{"type":"string"},"digest":{"type":"string"},"nextOmitted":{"description":"How many further `meta.next` steps were left out past the limit","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"policyApproved":{"type":"boolean"},"relay":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/schemas/ApprovalRelay"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Set when an agent recorded the approval for the human (0.32)."},"unchanged":{"description":"true when a repeat found its work already done with identical content and wrote nothing; absent otherwise","type":"boolean"},"waitingOn":{"additionalProperties":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"description":"With a declared role: how many steps each other owner holds (`human` for the steps only the human takes)","type":"object"}},"required":["change","brief","digest","approvedBy","policyApproved"],"title":"Approved","type":"object"},"ErrorBody":{"description":"The `error` member of a failure envelope. Field order is the document\norder: `code` first. An optional member with no value is left out of the\ndocument, so the body validates against the contract's error schema.","properties":{"code":{"description":"Stable SCREAMING_SNAKE code a caller branches on, registered in the tool's error registry.","type":"string"},"expected":{"description":"The valid values of `field`, when it takes a closed set.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":["array","null"]},"field":{"description":"The refused argv name (`--scenario`) or an RFC 6901 JSON pointer into `--input`.","type":["string","null"]},"hint":{"description":"A working invocation or the next step.","type":["string","null"]},"message":{"type":"string"},"reason":{"description":"Which of the situations registered under `code` this is (since 1.1); registered in the code's row.","type":["string","null"]},"received":{"description":"The value that was refused, with secrets redacted; `\"\"` for an empty value the caller sent (1.1).","type":["string","null"]},"retryable":{"description":"True only where running the same command again can succeed; equal to the registry row's.","type":"boolean"},"suggestions":{"description":"The nearest valid commands, options or values.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"}},"required":["code","message","retryable"],"type":"object"},"ItemStatus":{"description":"What happened to one element of a batch.","oneOf":[{"const":"written","description":"The element ran and wrote.","type":"string"},{"const":"unchanged","description":"The element ran and found its record already present with identical content.","type":"string"},{"const":"failed","description":"The element ran and failed; `error` says why.","type":"string"},{"const":"skipped","description":"An earlier element failed, so this one never ran.","type":"string"}]},"Outcome":{"description":"What happened to one id of a call with several ([`ApprovedMany`]).","oneOf":[{"const":"written","description":"The brief and the policy now carry the approval.","type":"string"},{"const":"unchanged","description":"They already carried this very approval: nothing was written.","type":"string"},{"const":"failed","description":"Writing this id failed (a disk error after the checks passed).","type":"string"},{"const":"skipped","description":"An earlier id failed to write, so this one was not tried.","type":"string"}]}},"x-canon":{"roles":[]}},"meta":{"command":"schema","schemaVersion":"1.1","tool":"canon","toolVersion":"0.33.0","contract":"atip/1","contractVersion":"1.1"}}
